          "style": "excalidraw",
          "accent": "violet",
          "decor": true
        },
        "presenterNotes": "- Timing: about 20 minutes of prepared material, including your closing section, then 10 minutes for questions.\n- OpenPoke separates the Interaction Agent, which talks to the user, from saved Execution Agents, which retain assigned work and history.\n- I focused on the ways saved agents, execution history, and concurrent work grow independently.\n- This walkthrough covers the implemented changes and the recorded results.\n- The original solution board remains on this canvas as the detailed reference."
      },
      "name": "01 — OpenPoke: Controlling agent overload"
    },
