      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "slidesOrder": 8,
        "mcpSlideLayout": "columns",
        "mcpSlideDesign": {
          "style": "excalidraw",
          "accent": "violet",
          "decor": true
        },
        "presenterNotes": "- About 1 minute. Offline tests check code behavior and regression safety; real-model evaluations check whether the agent actually completes the intended task.\n- The 196 pytest cases include evaluator infrastructure. Authored evaluation scenarios are a separate count, not 114 additional pytest cases.\n- The paired comparison fixes the chat model, synthetic mailbox, saved agents and user requests across upstream and fork. Outcomes are checked from tool traces and stored state, not judged by persuasive prose.\n- Dense retrieval uses real embeddings, ground-truth target IDs, recall@10/@30, and separately scored ambiguity cases. Selected full IA runs check final owner selection and clarification.\n- Memory compacts a 72-exchange journal using the real model, then requires exact facts, source reads and supported citations, no external write, and intact pending approval. Queue admission is tested separately using production SQLite paths with simulated completion.\n- Sources: README.md, docs/evaluation/README.md, the recorded result JSON files, and docs/charts/measurements.json."
      },
      "name": "09 — How I tested it"
    },
